    "title": "Infinitive, Gerund and Participle Constructions",
    "subtitle": "al + inf., sin + inf., perfect infinitive, gerund uses, absolute participle clauses",
    "footer": "Spanish Learning Program · B2 · Grammar · Infinitive, gerund, participle",
    "next": "Next: B2 · PDF 6 — Prepositions and verb + preposition"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "use the infinitive after prepositions (al + inf., sin + inf., por + inf., de + inf.)",
        "use the simple and perfect gerund for time, cause, manner and condition",
        "use absolute participle clauses (Terminada la reunión, ...)",
        "avoid the common gerund errors (the \"boiling water\" gerund)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. The infinitive"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        4.6,
        6.2,
        6.2
      ],
      "head": [
        "Structure",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "al + inf. (when)",
          "Al llegar, llamé a Ana.",
          "On arriving, I called Ana."
        ],
        [
          "al + inf. (cause)",
          "Al ser domingo, está cerrado.",
          "As it is Sunday, it is closed."
        ],
        [
          "sin + inf.",
          "Salió sin decir nada.",
          "He left without saying anything."
        ],
        [
          "por + inf. (cause)",
          "Lo despidieron por llegar tarde.",
          "They fired him for arriving late."
        ],
        [
          "por + inf. (not yet)",
          "La carta está por escribir.",
          "The letter is yet to be written."
        ],
        [
          "para + inf.",
          "Estudio para aprobar.",
          "I study to pass."
        ],
        [
          "de + inf. (condition)",
          "De llover, nos quedamos.",
          "If it rains, we stay."
        ],
        [
          "a + inf. (condition)",
          "A decir verdad, no me gusta.",
          "To tell the truth, I do not like it."
        ],
        [
          "después de / antes de + inf.",
          "Antes de salir, cierra la puerta.",
          "Before leaving, close the door."
        ],
        [
          "hasta + inf.",
          "Trabaja hasta caer rendido.",
          "He works until he drops."
        ],
        [
          "infinitive as subject",
          "Fumar es malo.",
          "Smoking is bad."
        ],
        [
          "el + inf. (noun)",
          "El fumar es malo. / El comer bien es sano.",
          "Smoking is bad. / Eating well is healthy."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "<b>Perfect infinitive</b> (haber + participle) shows an action <b>before</b> the main verb: <i>Dice haber llegado tarde.</i> (He says he arrived late.) <i>Después de haber comido, salimos.</i> <i>Me alegro de haberte conocido.</i>"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Same subject: infinitive",
      "text": "When both verbs share a subject, use the infinitive: <i>Quiero salir.</i> / <i>Me alegro de verte.</i> With different subjects use <b>que + subjunctive</b>: <i>Quiero que salgas. / Me alegro de que vengas.</i>"
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. The gerund"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        4.6,
        6.2,
        6.2
      ],
      "head": [
        "Use",
        "Example",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Simultaneous action",
          "Entró cantando.",
          "He came in singing."
        ],
        [
          "Manner",
          "Aprendió español viendo series.",
          "He learnt Spanish by watching series."
        ],
        [
          "Cause",
          "Siendo así, no puedo ir.",
          "That being so, I cannot go."
        ],
        [
          "Condition",
          "Estudiando, aprobarás.",
          "If you study, you will pass."
        ],
        [
          "Concession",
          "Aun siendo caro, lo compré.",
          "Even though it was expensive, I bought it."
        ],
        [
          "Time (sequence)",
          "Vio el accidente volviendo a casa.",
          "He saw the accident on the way home."
        ],
        [
          "Perfect gerund",
          "Habiendo terminado, se fue.",
          "Having finished, he left."
        ],
        [
          "Position",
          "Lo vi cruzando la calle.",
          "I saw him crossing the street."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warn",
      "title": "Gerund restrictions",
      "bullets": [
        "The gerund describes the <b>action</b> of the verb. To identify or describe a noun, use a relative clause: <i>Conozco a la chica que vive allí</i>, not <i>la chica viviendo allí</i>.",
        "Not for a following action as in English (\"he left, closing the door\") unless simultaneous: <i>Salió y cerró la puerta</i>.",
        "Not as an adjective: <i>agua hirviendo</i> is fixed; otherwise use a relative clause or adjective: <i>una caja que contiene ...</i>, not <i>una caja conteniendo ...</i>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Pronouns attach to the gerund: <i>mirándolo, diciéndomelo</i> (accent on the stressed vowel).",
        "Irregular gerunds: <i>diciendo, durmiendo, pidiendo, sintiendo, leyendo, oyendo, viniendo, yendo</i>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pagebreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "3. Absolute participle clauses"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A past participle can open a sentence and mean \"after / once ...\". The participle <b>agrees with the noun</b> that follows."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        6.0,
        6.0,
        5.0
      ],
      "head": [
        "Spanish",
        "English",
        "Pattern"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Terminada la reunión, salimos.",
          "Once the meeting was over, we left.",
          "participle + noun"
        ],
        [
          "Hecho esto, nos fuimos.",
          "That done, we left.",
          "participle + pronoun"
        ],
        [
          "Dicho esto, cerró la puerta.",
          "Having said this, he closed the door.",
          "set phrase"
        ],
        [
          "Una vez terminado el trabajo, descansó.",
          "Once the work was finished, he rested.",
          "una vez + participle"
        ],
        [
          "Cerradas las tiendas, volvimos.",
          "With the shops closed, we returned.",
          "agrees: feminine plural"
        ],
        [
          "Visto lo visto, me voy.",
          "Given what I have seen, I am leaving.",
          "set phrase"
        ],
        [
          "Acabado el curso, viajó.",
          "When the course ended, he travelled.",
          "participle + noun"
        ],
        [
          "Pasadas las diez, cierran.",
          "After ten o'clock, they close.",
          "pasado / pasadas"
        ]
      ]
    },
